---
import CodeTabs from "../../components/CodeTabs.astro";
import Pager from "../../components/Pager.astro";
import Picker from "../../components/Picker.astro";
import Page from "../../layouts/Page.astro";
---

<Page
  title="Styling · oklch-picker"
  description="Every value is a custom property, so a theme is set by overriding those rather than rewriting rules. Or skip the stylesheet entirely."
>
  <h1>Styling</h1>

  <p class="lede">
    <code>@oklch-picker/core/styles.css</code> is a starting point, not a
    requirement. Every element has a stable class name, so you can skip it
    entirely and write your own.
  </p>

  <p>If you do use it, the palette is custom properties on the root:</p>

  <CodeTabs
    name="palette"
    snippets={[
      {
        label: "Colours",
        lang: "css",
        code: `.oklch-picker {
  --okp-text: #1a1a1a;
  --okp-text-muted: #6b6b6b;
  --okp-line: #d8d8d8;
  --okp-surface: #ffffff;
  --okp-warn: #9a6b00;
  --okp-focus: #2f6fd0;
  --okp-thumb: #fff;
  --okp-thumb-line: rgb(0 0 0 / 0.55);
  --okp-segment-selected: #1a1a1a;
}`,
      },
      {
        label: "Metrics",
        lang: "css",
        code: `.oklch-picker {
  --okp-gap: 10px;
  --okp-radius: 6px;
  --okp-track-height: 12px;
  --okp-chart-height: 34px;
  --okp-chart-large-height: 180px;
  --okp-side-by-side-width: 560px;
  --okp-rail-width: 152px;
  --okp-thumb-size: 16px;

  /* A native range thumb is inset by half its width at each end, so
     everything positioned by value is inset to match. Change it only
     alongside --okp-thumb-size. */
  --okp-inset: calc(var(--okp-thumb-size) / 2);

  /* How strongly reference-gamut outlines are drawn on the chart. */
  --okp-boundary-opacity: 0.45;
}`,
      },
    ]}
  />

  <p>
    The <code>--okp-text</code> … <code>--okp-focus</code> colours are
    <code>light-dark()</code> pairs by default, so override them with a plain
    colour to pin one, or your own <code>light-dark()</code> pair to keep both
    schemes.
  </p>

  <h2>Colour scheme</h2>

  <p>
    It follows the system colour scheme by default. Set
    <code>data-theme="light"</code> or <code>data-theme="dark"</code> on the
    root element to pin one. That is what this site's own theme toggle does,
    so the pickers below follow the button in the header.
  </p>

  <Picker caption="Toggle the theme in the header and watch this follow." />

  <h2>Renaming the classes</h2>

  <p>
    Every class is prefixed, and the prefix is a prop. Change it and the
    stylesheet no longer applies, which is the point when you are writing your
    own:
  </p>

  <CodeTabs
    name="prefix"
    snippets={[
      {
        label: "React",
        lang: "tsx",
        code: `<ColourPicker value={colour} onChange={setColour} classPrefix="brand-picker" />`,
      },
      {
        label: "Vue",
        lang: "vue",
        code: `<ColourPicker v-model="colour" class-prefix="brand-picker" />`,
      },
      {
        label: "Svelte",
        lang: "svelte",
        code: `<ColourPicker bind:value={colour} classPrefix="brand-picker" />`,
      },
      {
        label: "Solid",
        lang: "tsx",
        code: `<ColourPicker value={colour()} onChange={setColour} classPrefix="brand-picker" />`,
      },
      {
        label: "Angular",
        lang: "html",
        code: `<oklch-colour-picker
  [value]="colour()"
  (valueChange)="colour.set($event)"
  classPrefix="brand-picker"
/>`,
      },
      {
        label: "Qwik",
        lang: "tsx",
        code: `<ColourPicker
  value={colour.value}
  onChange$={$((c: string) => (colour.value = c))}
  classPrefix="brand-picker"
/>`,
      },
      {
        label: "Astro",
        lang: "astro",
        code: `<oklch-picker class-prefix="brand-picker"></oklch-picker>`,
      },
      {
        label: "No framework",
        lang: "html",
        code: `<oklch-picker class-prefix="brand-picker"></oklch-picker>`,
      },
    ]}
  />

  <p>
    <code>className</code> adds a class to the root element without replacing
    the prefix, for the common case of one-off spacing.
  </p>

  <div class="note">
    <p>
      The custom element renders into the light DOM, so the stylesheet and any
      <code>--okp-*</code> override applies exactly as it does for the framework
      adapters, which also means it is not style-isolated.
    </p>
  </div>

  <Pager />
</Page>
